@noindent
and a new clause in the dispatch in @code{analyze}

@example typescript
    case "require":
      return analyzeRequire(expr, analyze);
@end example

@noindent
as well the procedure @code{analyzeRequire} that handles @code{require}
expressions.  Complete the following definition of @code{analyzeRequire}.

@example typescript
export const analyzeRequire = (
  expr: Expr,
  analyze: AmbAnalyze
): AmbExecute => @{
  const condition = requirePredicate(expr);
  const test: Expr =
    condition === undefined
      ? @{ tag: "boolean", value: false, span: expr.span @}
      : condition;
  const pproc = analyze(test);
  return (env, succeed, fail) =>
    pproc(
      env,
      (predValue, fail2) => (predValue === true
        ? succeed(undefined, fail2)
        : fail2()),
      fail,
    );
@};
@end example
@end quotation

@quotation
@strong{In this language: nondeterministic computing.}

The search experiment extends the guest language with the @code{choose},
@code{require}, and @code{ramb} nodes only, and runs under the named modes
@code{amb-depth-firstExperiment} and @code{amb-ramb-experiment}.  Execution
procedures carry a success and a failure continuation; assignment is undone on
backtracking unless the program asks for a permanent write; the core language
and the native runtime remain eager and deterministic.
@end quotation

